// Same-step guard compensation with an ANCHOR-SHARED correlation var — the
// classical (non-GuardRel) sibling of the 0904 family's same-step gap.
//
// `Heartbeat{server: x} since Login{server: x}` requires an UNBROKEN
// per-server heartbeat streak since that server's login. The DSQL backend's
// guard streak is correctly keyed per server, but its SAME-STEP compensation
// (the streak-extend CTE's write is snapshot-invisible, so "the guard fires
// NOW" is checked with an inline EXISTS over the current batch) tested only
// the guard's predicate SHAPE — not that the event's `server` matches the
// anchor row being validated.
//
// @30 is the trap: server s1's streak is alive through @20, and a heartbeat
// fires at @30 — but for server s2. The unconstrained EXISTS wrongly extends
// s1's streak → over-PERMIT; the interpreter denies (s1's streak broke at
// @30, and s2 has no Login anchor). @10/@20 are the over-constraint
// controls: a MATCHING same-step heartbeat must keep permitting.
//
// Interpreter is the oracle (see expected_1.out). Found by independent
// review of the temporal-compiler same-step guard compensation.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (x: String). (
        Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat"::request{ input.server: x }
        since within 1h
        Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.server: x }
    )
};
